russian-language-data
=====================

This repository redistributes and builds upon third-party data. Per the
CC BY-SA 4.0 ShareAlike terms, the datasets in this repository (the files under
data/) are themselves licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
International (CC BY-SA 4.0) — see the LICENSE file.

Sources and attribution
-----------------------

1. OpenRussian (https://en.openrussian.org/, https://github.com/Badestrand/russian-dictionary)
   Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.
   Used to build:
     - data/stress-db.json          (word -> stress-marked form)
     - data/aspect-pairs-db.json    (imperfective/perfective verb pairs)
     - data/aspect-db.json          (verb aspect + pairs; with OpenCorpora, below)
     - data/translations/en.json    (English dictionary entries)
     - data/translations/de.json    (German dictionary entries)
   Changes made: the source CSV tables were parsed, filtered, deduplicated and
   reshaped into two JSON lookup files; apostrophe stress marks were converted
   to the combining acute accent (U+0301); placeholder/noise headwords were
   dropped. See scripts/build-language-db.mjs for the exact transformation.

2. WikDict (https://www.wikdict.com/)
   Licensed under CC BY-SA 3.0, built from Wiktionary via DBnary.
   Used to build:
     - data/translations/fr.json, es.json, it.json, nl.json, zh.json
   Changes made: the per-pair SQLite dictionaries were read, low-confidence
   pairs (WikDict score below 20) and non-word headwords were dropped, the
   gloss list was split and capped at six entries, and the result reshaped into
   the JSON lookup files above. See scripts/build-translations.mjs.

3. OpenCorpora (http://opencorpora.org/)
   Licensed under CC BY-SA. The morphological dictionary behind pymorphy3.
   Used to build:
     - data/aspect-db.json          (the aspect grammeme of every verb lemma,
                                     and the check that flips or drops a
                                     contradictory OpenRussian pair)
   Changes made: verb lemmas were extracted from the dictionary, bucketed by
   aspect, merged with the OpenRussian pairs and reshaped into the JSON lookup
   file above. See scripts/build-aspect-db.py. The OpenCorpora dictionary
   itself is not included in this repository; it is also queried at runtime by
   consumers of this data.

